  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Papuan Women&apos;s Empowerment Project (PAWE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the Project is to empower poor women in Papua by increasing their participation in implementation and decision-making processes in the community driven development program (PNPM Rural and RESPEK) so that they are better able to benefit from the program and address their needs and priorities through i) strengthening existing women&apos;s organizations and networks to provide leadershipcomma trainingcomma and advocacy to women at the village levelcomma ii) building capacity of individual women through demand driven capacitybuilding and training opportunitiescomma iii) building awareness and capacity of PNPM Rural/RESPEK project staff and other key stakeholders such as village leaders and government officials to promote greater gender equality.</narrative>
  </description>
